From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sigivb72-netizen <vergilx63@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 06:36:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] podot: servers, scene, modules: clear singletons and
 registries on teardown

Needed to set the engine up again in the same process (in-process
instances): singletons clear their pointer in their destructor, the
rendering server globals (RSG) are cleared after the renderer is
finalized, and registries filled at every setup (movie writers, scene
idle callbacks, navigation server managers) are reset or de-duplicated.

Touch gestures: ViewPanner accepts pan gestures (it handled them but
let them propagate), and the 3D viewport pans with unmodified pan
gestures on touchscreens (two-finger drag).

InProcessGame (scene/main): runs a project's scene in a second SceneTree
inside the editor process, next to the open editor (platforms that can't
start a game process). Its root Window renders off-screen
(Window::set_offscreen_root()); game code runs with editor hint off and
scripting on; the editor's physics spaces are paused while it runs; the
project's input actions and autoloads are added for the game's lifetime.

Audio: the Dummy driver clears its buffer pointer in finish().
AudioServer::finish() finishes every registered driver on each teardown,
so a second in-process teardown freed the buffer again (abort when
pressing Play on iPadOS).
